---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="About — Drone Max Wind"
	description="Why Drone Max Wind exists: a free, mobile-first go / no-go wind check for consumer drones in the US."
>
	<Header />
	<main class="page-wrap max-w-3xl py-16">
		<p class="font-mono text-caption uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">About</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-display-lg font-semibold text-ink">Built for the field, not the desk.</h1>
		<p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-body">
			Most wind tools either hide 80 m and 120 m behind a paywall, ask you to type a rating you
			do not remember, or publish a 2,000-word essay. We built a{" "}
			<a href="/#calculator" class="text-link">calculator</a> that already knows the airframe
			and speaks in go / no-go. See{" "}
			<a href="/how-it-works" class="text-link">how it works</a>.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-body">
			Wind comes from Open-Meteo. Model limits come from manufacturer specs when they publish
			them — browse the{" "}
			<a href="/models" class="text-link">model database</a> or read{" "}
			<a href="/drone-wind-resistance" class="text-link">what wind resistance means</a>. Holy
			Stone and a few cinema frames are labeled as class estimates. This is a planning aid, not
			an FAA product.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-body">
			Domain: <span class="font-mono text-sm">dronemaxwind.com</span>. Operated as an independent
			utility — not an FAA product, not affiliated with DJI or other makers. The check is
			informational; weather can change, and you remain responsible for the flight.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-8">
			<a href="/#calculator" class="font-medium text-link">Open the calculator →</a>
			{" · "}
			<a href="/contact" class="font-medium text-link">Contact</a>
			{" · "}
			<a href="/terms" class="font-medium text-link">Terms</a>
		</p>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
